 "remarks": "Don't let the square footage fool you - this home lives large. Tucked into a lovely, walkable neighborhood perfect for evening strolls and bike rides, this is a home that punches well above its size, with all the essentials thoughtfully in place. The main level sets the tone, LR w/high ceilings opens to the kitchen for an open flow that feels bright and spacious. Just a short flight up, three bedrooms share their own private level. Downstairs, a large family room with a fireplace anchors the lower level, alongside a fourth bedroom that flexes easily as a home office. The basement adds laundry and abundant storage, with plenty of untapped potential to finish. Outside, a cozy screened-in porch is made for lazy summer evenings and movie nights. And there's room to grow: expand above the oversized two-car garage for a primary suite retreat, or enclose the porch to create a formal dining room - the footprint here has real potential to stretch further. Best of all, the hard work is already done. Fresh exterior paint, a new roof, and many recent updates mean this home is truly move-in ready. With 5mins to train and I95, 6mins to Compo beach, 5mins to downtown Main St. this location is hard to beat.",
